title: Add pallet-pgas-allowance with ChargePGAS transaction extension
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      ## Summary

      - Introduces `pallet-pgas-allowance` providing a new `ChargePGAS<T, S>` transaction
        extension that wraps an inner fee extension `S`.
      - When a signed transaction dispatches a call matching `Config::CallFilter` and the
        signer holds enough PGAS (a trusted asset on Asset Hub), the fee is withdrawn as
        a `fungibles::Credit`. In `post_dispatch` the credit is split: the `actual_fee`
        portion is dropped (burning total issuance via `OnDropCredit`) and the unused
        remainder is `resolve`d back to the payer. Otherwise the inner extension runs
        unchanged.
      - Wires the extension into `asset-hub-westend` around `ChargeAssetTxPayment`, with
        the filter matching `pallet-revive` calls and PGAS bound to
        `AssetIdForTrustBackedAssets = 0`.

      ## Flow

      1. `validate`: unsigned origin or filter miss -> delegate to inner. Signed + filter
         hit + `reducible_balance(PGAS, Preserve) >= fee` -> tag as PGAS path.
      2. `prepare`: `Balanced::withdraw(fee, Preservation::Preserve)` -> `Credit` stored
         in `Pre::PGAS`. Using `Preserve` keeps at least the asset's existential deposit
         in the payer's account.
      3. `post_dispatch_details`: split `Credit` by `actual_fee`; `resolve` refund to
         payer; drop consumed portion (burns issuance).

      The imbalance-based flow mirrors `FungibleAdapter::correct_and_deposit_fee` in
      `pallet-transaction-payment`.

      ## Benchmarks

      Two benchmarks measure the extension overhead:
      - `charge_pgas`: full PGAS path (validate + withdraw credit + resolve refund).
      - `charge_pgas_skip`: PGAS path skipped (validation preamble only, falls through
        to the inner extension).

      `weight()` reserves the worst case (`charge_pgas`); `post_dispatch_details`
      refunds the difference when the skip path is taken.

      ## Test plan

      - [x] `cargo test -p pallet-pgas-allowance --features runtime-benchmarks` - 10 tests:
        - `pgas_pays_for_filtered_call_with_zero_native`
        - `falls_back_to_inner_when_no_pgas`
        - `filter_miss_uses_inner_even_with_pgas`
        - `pgas_refund_on_unused_weight`
        - `pgas_below_ed_falls_back_to_native`
        - `unsigned_delegates_to_inner`
        - `bench_charge_pgas`, `bench_charge_pgas_skip`
        - mock construct-runtime integrity + genesis builder
      - [x] `cargo check -p asset-hub-westend-runtime --features runtime-benchmarks`
      - [ ] CI runs full workspace build / clippy / tests
crates:
  - name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
    bump: minor
  - name: pallet-pgas-allowance
    bump: minor
